#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# print

#% text
# `print(x)` writes `x` as a line of output and gives `x` itself.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A string is written as its text, without quotes; any other value in its printed form.

#% item
# The line is output of the evaluation, shown before the value of the cell; a cell can print many lines.

#% item
# Because the value is `x`, `print` can be wrapped around any part of a computation to watch it without changing the result.

#% item
# `print` takes one argument. To print several values on one line, use `say`, which joins its arguments and gives `null`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
print("Hello")
#% output
#| Hello
#= "Hello"

#% text
# The value is printed and also returned:

#% cell
print(1/3 + 1/6)
#% output
#| 1/2
#= 1/2

#% text
# Several lines from one cell, then its value:

#% cell
print("first"); print("second"); 42
#% output
#| first
#| second
#= 42

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic expressions and lists:

#% cell
print(integrate(x*exp(x), x));
#% output
#| -exp(x) + x*exp(x)
#= -exp(x) + x*exp(x)

#% cell
print(table(k^2, k, 5));
#% output
#| [1, 4, 9, 16, 25]
#= [1, 4, 9, 16, 25]

#% text
# A machine real prints with the digits needed to read it back, a ball with its correct digits:

#% cell
print(0.1 + 0.2); print(n(pi, 30));
#% output
#| 0.30000000000000004
#| 3.1415926535897932384626433832795029
#= 3.1415926535897932384626433832795029

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Watching an iteration from inside a loop:

#% cell
{
  var x = 1.0
  for k in range(4) {
    x = print((x + 2/x)/2)
  }
}
#% output
#| 1.5
#| 1.4166666666666665
#| 1.4142156862745097
#| 1.4142135623746899

#% text
# Seeing the intermediate value of a nested computation:

#% cell
sqrt(print(3^2 + 4^2))
#% output
#| 25
#= 5

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `print(x)` gives `x`:

#% cell
print(7) === 7
#% output
#| 7
#= true

#% text
# `say` joins several parts on one line and gives `null`:

#% cell
say("k = ", 3, ", k^2 = ", 9)
#% output
#| k = 3, k^2 = 9

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# With more than one argument, `print` prints nothing and the call stays as it is:

#% cell
print("x =", 2)
#% output
#= print("x =", 2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `say`, `to_string`, `message`, `timing`
